# ============================================================ 2. CORE BRAND HIERARCHY

Establish this hierarchy:

OX-DX
│
├── Universal Ontology & Experience Engine
│ │
│ └── Universal Ontology Engine
│
├── OX-DX Specification
│
├── OX-DX Tools
│
├── OX-DX Interfaces
│
├── OX-DX Documentation
│
└── OX-DX Community

```

Explain the hierarchy carefully.

IMPORTANT:

OX-DX is the umbrella brand/system identity.

"Universal Ontology & Experience Engine" is the public conceptual product descriptor.

"Universal Ontology Engine" is the current technical engine implementation.

These are related but must not be treated as interchangeable arbitrary names.

============================================================
3. BRAND VS PRODUCT VS REPOSITORY
============================================================

Define this distinction explicitly.

BRAND:
OX-DX

PRODUCT / SYSTEM:
Universal Ontology & Experience Engine

IMPLEMENTATION:
Universal Ontology Engine

REPOSITORY:
universal-ontology-engine

PACKAGE / CRATE:
existing technical package names

WEBSITE:
future OX-DX public web property

DOCUMENTATION:
OX-DX Docs

Make this a core naming rule.

A repository name does not automatically define the public brand.

============================================================
4. BRAND ARCHITECTURE MODEL
============================================================

Use:

                OX-DX
                  │
       ┌──────────┼──────────┐
       │          │          │
     ENGINE     SPECS      TOOLS
       │          │          │
       │          │          ├── CLI
       │          │          ├── inspectors
       │          │          └── utilities
       │          │
       │          ├── ontology
       │          └── schemas
       │
       ├── runtime/resolution
       ├── graph
       ├── discovery
       └── language adapters

Then:

INTERFACES
DOCS
COMMUNITY

Do not force every future capability into this exact structure if a clearer model emerges from repository evidence.

============================================================
5. BRAND LAYERS
============================================================

Define six layers.

### LAYER 1 — OX-DX BRAND

The identity users recognize.

### LAYER 2 — PRODUCTS / SYSTEMS

Major user-facing systems under OX-DX.

### LAYER 3 — ENGINES

Core computational implementations.

### LAYER 4 — TOOLS

CLI, inspectors, generators, converters, utilities.

### LAYER 5 — INTERFACES

Web, UI, API, visualization.

### LAYER 6 — INFRASTRUCTURE / IMPLEMENTATION

Packages, crates, libraries, schemas, internal modules.

Explain why these layers must not be conflated.

