7. REPOSITORY NAMING POLICY
============================================================

Create:

`assets/documentation/architecture/repository-naming.md`

Define how future OX-DX repositories should be named.

General rule:

Public family:

`ox-dx-*`

Technical implementation names may remain descriptive where useful.

Examples of future patterns:

`ox-dx-web`
`ox-dx-docs`
`ox-dx-cli`
`ox-dx-sdk`

BUT:

Do not rename existing repositories just to satisfy this convention.

Legacy/current names remain valid unless a deliberate migration is approved.

Explain when to use:

`ox-dx-*`

versus:

descriptive technical repository names.

Avoid repository-name explosion.

============================================================
8. PACKAGE / CRATE NAMING
============================================================

Create:

`assets/documentation/architecture/package-naming.md`

Define rules for:

Rust crates
NPM packages
CLI binaries
libraries

For Rust:

Prefer implementation-oriented names.

Example:

`ontology-core`
`ontology-graph`

Do NOT force every crate to become:

`ox-dx-*`

because crates should remain technically descriptive.

Brand belongs above implementation names.

This is an important boundary.

